Kimi K3 SiTU, static checkpoint input scales and an optional pre-dispatched
launch for DeepGEMM's SM100 NVFP4 Mega MoE kernel (sm100_nvfp4_mega_moe.cuh).
Applied by cmake/external_projects/deepgemm.cmake to the pinned DeepGEMM
checkout only when VLLM_K31_NVFP4_SITU_PATCH is ON (default OFF).

Build it only for Kimi K3 images: the patched header computes SiTU in place
of the SwiGLU epilogue, so every 'swiglu' launch of this kernel becomes SiTU
(alpha * tanh(gate / alpha) * sigmoid(gate) * beta * tanh(up / beta), with
activation_alpha / activation_beta as the SiTU scales). Other NVFP4 Mega MoE
models must use a build without it.

- SiTU: the expression and helpers of sm100_fp8_fp4_mega_moe_situ.cuh (the
  stock FP8 x FP4 SiTU kernel); kFastMath (stock default true) selects __expf
  and fast_rcp as there, and tanh is 2 * sigmoid(2x) - 1.
- Static input scales: with use_x_scales=false each local expert's L2 input
  scale is read from the otherwise unused local x-scales region; launches
  with use_x_scales=true are unchanged.
- Pre-dispatch (M1): a launch whose dispatch head already ran (signalled in a
  spare word of the expert send counts) skips the token counting and waits
  for each source rank's input-ready epoch before pulling from it. Static
  asserts: kNumExperts <= kNumMaxExperts - 128 and kNumRanks <= 32.

vLLM selects these paths with K31_NVFP4_SITU_HEADER=1 (and K31_NVFP4_CKPT_SCALES,
K31_M1); without the flag the Python side refuses SiTU on this kernel.

